==============================================================================
O24 — prime-generator orbit  (fit-free; exact counts; projection, not fit)
==============================================================================
  O18 showed the integer bases are blind to the zeros SINGLY but not JOINTLY: at
  x0 = 2 the pure dyadic and pure triadic ladders returned NULL, while the joint
  orbit {2^m 3^n} detected gamma_2 at P/median 6.95 and {2^m 3^n 5^k} detected
  gamma_4 at 16.37. Only PRIME bases add generators: 4, 8 and 9 lie inside the
  semigroup 2 and 3 already generate, so they do not densify the orbit. This script
  makes the generator set a PARAMETER and sweeps the NESTED family on identical
  settings, to measure how detection scales with the number of prime generators and
  whether it saturates. Interpretation of the numbers below is NOT this script's job.

  x0 = 2   xmax = 3000000000   dps = 30   surrogates = 200   seed = 2026
  generators = 2,3,5,7,11,13,17,19   nested family:
    G1 = {2}
    G2 = {2, 3}
    G3 = {2, 3, 5}
    G4 = {2, 3, 5, 7}
    G5 = {2, 3, 5, 7, 11}
    G6 = {2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13}
    G7 = {2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17}
    G8 = {2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19}
  pi/log2 = 4.532360     pi/log3 = 2.859601

